  {
   "lead": "Korea had its second brutal day in a row, and it is your largest single exposure.",
   "text": "KOSPI closed Friday 6.02% lower at 5,059.69 after a 5.28% fall on Thursday. Samsung dropped 6.35% and SK hynix 10.44%. Your dashboard prices SCBKEQTG at its 4 Nov NAV this morning, so most of this is not in your numbers yet.",
   "dir": "neg",
   "exposure_pct": 17.0,
   "exposure_label": "Korea"
  },
  {
   "lead": "A very strong US jobs report raised the odds of another Fed rate rise in December.",
   "text": "US employers added 165,000 jobs in October against about 59,000 expected, and unemployment slipped to 4.1%. Markets now put a December rate rise at roughly 77%. The 10-year yield ended Friday near 4.86%.",
   "dir": "watch",
   "exposure_pct": 16.9,
   "exposure_label": "United States"
  },
  {
