  {
   "id": "kospi-second-day-rout",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "Korean shares sink again as chip stocks take another beating",
   "when": "Fri 6 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "KOSPI fell 324.11 points, or 6.02%, to 5,059.69, after dropping 5.28% the day before. It was down more than 8% at one point, went below 5,000 and triggered a 20-minute trading halt, then recovered to close above that level. Samsung Electronics lost 6.35% and SK hynix 10.44%. Kosdaq fell 5.03% to 644.27.",
   "why": "Korea is about 17% of the portfolio, almost all in SCBKEQTG, a fund that holds the big chipmakers. Dashboard prices for SCBKEQTG and EWY lag this move: the fund shows its 4 Nov NAV, and the dashboard refreshes again at 11:30, when newer NAVs usually arrive. The KOSPI is down about 11% since that date.",
