   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Hiring far beats forecasts, firming up expectations of a December Fed hike",
   "when": "Fri 6 Nov · 08:30 ET",
   "what": "Nonfarm payrolls rose by 165,000 in October. Unemployment was 4.1% and hourly earnings rose 0.4% to $38.00. August and September were revised up by a combined 84,000. Fed funds futures priced a hike of a quarter point at the 9 Dec meeting at about 77%, up from about 66% a day earlier. The 10-year yield rose to about 4.86%. The S&P 500 closed up 0.31% and the Nasdaq up 1.09%.",
   "why": "Higher expected rates tend to weigh on richly valued US shares and on bond prices. The S&P 500 funds you hold are priced at 4 Nov NAV this morning, before Thursday's sharp tech fall; the index is about 4% lower than at that date.",
